[hermes:err-live] ### pytorch/pytorch#191596 — [BugFix] Fix operator precedence bug in check_channel signal pad validation
[hermes:err-live] - State: `CLOSED` · Closing-link from PR: no · Source: `hash`
[hermes:err-live] - URL: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/191596
[hermes:err-live] - Author: ASCII-S
[hermes:err-live] - Labels: triaged, open source, Merged, ciflow/trunk, release notes: distributed (c10d), ciflow/h100-symm-mem
[hermes:err-live] #### Issue body
[hermes:err-live] ### Problem
[hermes:err-live] `check_channel()` computes the channel upper bound as:
[hermes:err-live] ```cpp
[hermes:err-live] signal_pad_size / sizeof(uint32_t) * world_size
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] Due to C++ operator precedence (`/` and `*` have equal precedence and are
[hermes:err-live] left-associative), this is evaluated as:
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] (signal_pad_size / sizeof(uint32_t)) * world_size  =  N * world_size
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] The signal slot address used by `barrier`/`put_signal`/`wait_signal` is:
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] signal_pads[target] + world_size * channel + rank
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] i.e. the pad is indexed as `pad[channel][peer]` with a row length of
[hermes:err-live] `world_size`.  The no-OOB condition at `rank = world_size - 1` is:
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] world_size * channel + (world_size - 1) < N
[hermes:err-live] ⟺ (channel + 1) * world_size <= N
[hermes:err-live] ⟺ channel < N / world_size
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] The bound should therefore be `N / world_size`, not `N * world_size`.  As
[hermes:err-live] written the check is `world_size^2` times too permissive and does not
[hermes:err-live] prevent out-of-bounds access past the end of the signal pad.
[hermes:err-live] With default settings (`signal_pad_size = 32 * 72 * 4 = 9216` → `N = 2304`,
[hermes:err-live] `world_size = 8`): correct max channel = 288, but the buggy check allows up
[hermes:err-live] to 18432.
[hermes:err-live] ### Consequences
[hermes:err-live] An out-of-bounds `channel` argument can:
[hermes:err-live] - Land on an unmapped page → **CUDA error: an illegal memory access**
[hermes:err-live] - Land inside an adjacent allocation → **silent memory corruption** (worse)
[hermes:err-live] ### Fix
[hermes:err-live] Add parentheses to enforce the intended evaluation order:
[hermes:err-live] ```diff
[hermes:err-live] - signal_pad_size / sizeof(uint32_t) * world_size;
[hermes:err-live] + signal_pad_size / (sizeof(uint32_t) * world_size);
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] This only tightens the bound to exactly what's safe — every channel value
[hermes:err-live] that was legal before remains legal after the fix.
[hermes:err-live] ### Repro
[hermes:err-live] ```python
[hermes:err-live] import torch
[hermes:err-live] import torch.distributed as dist
[hermes:err-live] import torch.distributed._symmetric_memory as symm_mem
[hermes:err-live] # 2-GPU repro
[hermes:err-live] dist.init_process_group("nccl")
[hermes:err-live] torch.cuda.set_device(dist.get_rank())
[hermes:err-live] t = symm_mem.empty(64, device="cuda")
[hermes:err-live] hdl = symm_mem.rendezvous(t, group=dist.group.WORLD)
[hermes:err-live] # N = 2304, ws = 2 → max valid channel = 1152
[hermes:err-live] # channel=2000 → offset = 2*2000 + rank >= 4000 > 2304 → OOB
[hermes:err-live] hdl.barrier(channel=2000)
[hermes:err-live] torch.cuda.synchronize()
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] ### Test
[hermes:err-live] `test_barrier_channel_out_of_bounds` verifies that:
[hermes:err-live] - `channel == N / world_size` is rejected with a RuntimeError
[hermes:err-live] - `channel == N / world_size - 1` is accepted
